    "text": "There is an old Chinese saying: “No one who rises before dawn 360 days a year fails to make his family rich.”\nWe read it carefully. We thought about it deeply. And then we went back to sleep.\nOur team believes in a slightly updated version: why wake up before dawn to get rich, when you can let compound interest do the work while you sleep? That leaves 5 spare days a year for sunrises, and we are still deciding whether to use them.\nSo we are not against success. We just schedule it for after 10 a.m.\n\n\n\n\nEmma K. Adams\nThe American\n\n\n\n\n\nMarc Friedrich von Haas\nThe German"
